      "rationale": "Advisor-unavailable exception, feature sprint-alfred-epic, runner claude (native Windows), design revision 5.\n\nReceipt-backed fact<machine-path> The Advisor stage for this candidate (commit 48733052d) was run through the course producer for runner\n   claude. In this Pipeline version the course has no wired Advisor route for runner claude: the native\n   initial-Advisor entry recorded unavailability before any child or export (terminal no-child outcome,\n   code native-initial-answer-provenance-unavailable, no input submitted). The course binding and failure\n   evidence are the exported artifacts referenced by this package. Delivering that route is part of the\n   approved scope (Spec section 21.4, role-route preflight); a fallback consult may supply only a\n   labelled, non-authorizing Advisor input and never satisfies readiness, Critic or plan-verifier.\n2. Revision 5 was opened on a second device after a device switch: the approval-bound revision-4 package\n   lived in the ignored root evidence directory and is absent on this device, so the revision-4 approval\n   could not be verified here. The revision adds the PO decisions of 2026-10-06 and 2026-10-07\n   (design-input.md, decisions 17-26) and Spec section 22 (R7, agent-recoverable operation and device\n   portability, R7-1 to R7-11).\n3. This course is a new course for the revised design bound to the registered revision-5 authoring\n   dispatch and the revised source digests. No earlier course, Advisor or readiness evidence is reused.\n4. Independent readiness for this candidate is a separate, host-observed claude CLI child with its own\n   receipt in this package; the Advisor exception does not substitute for it.\n\nWhat this exception asks the PO to accept, once, at the final plan approval: that this design is\napproved without an Advisor answer because the course has no wired Advisor route for runner claude in\nthis version. It grants no other authority.\n"
    },
