  "summary": "Fresh comparison of the five sources against the candidate (commit 48733052…, tree 268e019e…). Mechanical checks pass: the PRD technical-spec-sha256 marker equals the Spec digest (3e5f9410…), and the 77-ID register map reconciles with the Spec §21 headers (R1 13, R2 8, R3 11, R4 20, R5 16, R6 6, deferred 3). The T1–T20 map reconciles between Spec §22.0 and traceability (15 R7-owned, 5 mapped, 20 total). PRD, Spec and traceability carry decisions 17–26 and R7-1…R7-11 consistently. Two blocking issues remain. (1) design.md was not updated for revision 5: it states a 17-row map, twelve rows owned by eight contracts, and no T18–T20, decisions 20–26, R7-10, R7-11 or R7 sequencing, which contradicts the other four sources. (2) Spec §22.10 branch (A) permits signature-free supersede of an earlier-revision registration for any owner state, including live and unavailable. That rule is not covered by PO decisions #22 or #23, which traceability cites for it, and it is in tension with the §20 no-inference rule. Non-blocking points: the unreconciled R7-6 pre-signing check against the R3 one-command-per-decision rule; an exception rationale wider than §21.4 permits; distilled, non-verbatim input; this revision's own evidence in the ignored root; stale decision counts in the PRD; AC rows and acceptance.md not in the package; the R7-11/R4 same-lock overlap; and unverified external claims. No Advisor answer exists: the course ended unavailable with no child started, and the proposed exception is non-authorizing. This report grants no approval or implementation authority.",
