{
  "candidate": {
    "commit": "8f476711a64437a09cb89044528f143faee008aa",
    "tree": "49e2b60183387929857d407a61f299e1f26acaa2"
  },
  "dispatchId": "ALFRED-READINESS-R5C-20261007",
  "findings": [
    {
      "code": "R76-TWO-COMMANDS-VS-213",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "summary": "Spec §21.3 says the PO receives one command per decision, and §21.0 says the R3-1 ceremony inventory counts any PO terminal command as a PO interaction. Spec §22.6 (R7-6, d(ii)) hands the PO a read-only readiness-check command first and the signing command only afterwards, in the same terminal. §22.0 and R7-6d(iv) claim R7 adds no interaction and that §§1-21 are not relaxed. These cannot all hold. §21.3, R3-1/R3-5 and §22.6 need one explicit reconciliation, for example 'one signing command preceded by one read-only check, both counted inside the single interaction', so the R3 inventory test and the R7-6 case do not fail each other."
    },
    {
      "code": "T20-DECISION-PROVENANCE-EXTERNAL",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "summary": "Spec §22.0 and §22.11 base the T20 contract (bootstrap receipt recorded at SubagentStart) on a 'PO decision bootstrap receipt option B' that lives in specs/sprint-alfred-epic/plans/po-decisions-2026-10-06.md. That file is not one of the five sources. design-input.md decision #26 covers only the lock contention (T19) and never mentions T20 or SubagentStart. The traceability decision table says 'T20 via the SubagentStart receipt' under #26 without any recorded input behind it. PRD §14 and design-input.md (2026-10-03 #1) say no separate document carries binding force beyond the approved sources. The decision must be recorded in design-input.md and in the traceability decision map, or the requirement must be dropped or marked as an unconfirmed proposal."
    },
    {
      "code": "COMPLETION-BOUNDARY-OMITS-R7",
      "severity": "non-blocking",
      "summary": "design.md 'Completion boundary' names PRD §7 and Spec §§12-21. PRD §7 has no item for the device-switch workstream, and Spec §13 Epic-complete refers only to the PRD §7 list. Only Spec §22.12 and the traceability row for AC-37 make R7 completion conditional. Decision #18 says the findings are fixed in 0.7.0 and not deferred, so epic completion should explicitly include AC-37 and R7-1a…R7-11e."
    },
    {
