ion token other than 2.56.0.windows.1. The attended prerequisite field shape is not named, so only exactly-one-form plus a non-empty string is asserted.\nR7-7c is partial: prepare-for-signature is driven with an unknown request digest (a seeded ceremony fixture is out of scope), so it pins that the report appears before the request lookup and that no signIntentCommand, authorizeBySignatureCommand or expiresAt is handed over; the signing-window semantics of 21.3 are not exercised. R7-7e also covers the spec's foreign-hook half. Catalogue admission of argv (21.1) is not pinned.\n4. Not changed: production code, schema, hard-coded test-count line was changed to cases.length (see deviations); scratch/ is ignored.\n5. Deviations: afterTests line changed from a literal 33 total to cases.length; stub git injected through runProbeFn and resolveTrustedExecutableFn (a real stub file for identity, spawn stubbed, because win32 cannot spawn a script stub); I issued one block of three parallel reads early (no lock error); one copyCommand.posix was refused for its newline, the single-line command field was used for stage and commit.\n6. Open: verify: pending; independent review: pending; PO acceptance: open; R7-7d not in scope."
